{
  "name": "Publish operational assessment microsite content from Supabase",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "9b17411b-a233-4377-85a4-7c38305b82d0",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        16,
        192
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 560,
        "height": 896,
        "content": "## Publish operational assessment microsite content from Supabase\n\n### Who’s it for\n\nThis template is for consultants, operations teams and automation builders who want to turn approved assessment records into structured content for client-facing microsites.\n\n### How it works\n\n1. Fetches approved assessment records from Supabase.\n2. Validates the company, microsite slug and assessment summary.\n3. Builds a reusable microsite content object with findings, opportunities, next steps and a call to action.\n4. Upserts the content into a Supabase `microsites` table using the slug as the unique key.\n5. Marks the source assessment as published or failed and records the public microsite URL or error.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- [ ] Create the two Supabase tables using the supplied schema.\n- [ ] Create/select a Supabase API credential in every Supabase HTTP Request node.\n- [ ] Edit `Set Microsite Settings` with your project URL, table names and public site URLs.\n- [ ] Add one safe test record with `status = approved`.\n- [ ] Run `Test Manually` and confirm the new row appears in `microsites`.\n- [ ] Confirm your website renders the `microsites` table at the URL pattern you configured.\n- [ ] Activate the six-hour schedule only after the manual test passes.\n\n### Requirements\n\nSupabase, n8n and a website/front end that renders the published `microsites` records.\n\n### Customization\n\nChange the source fields, default card copy, opportunity ideas, CTA, schedule, batch size and front-end route. Proprietary scoring, outreach logic and private assessment benchmarks are intentionally not included."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "90a03f18-f8b8-4858-9826-d0d91f37f0ca",
      "name": "Sticky Note1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        672,
        304
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 768,
        "height": 512,
        "content": "## Configure and fetch assessments\n\nRun manually while setting up, or every six hours in production. Set the Supabase project URL, table names, public microsite URL, booking URL and batch size, then fetch records whose status is approved."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "70014121-ce05-4edd-9a61-b9700b55e8df",
      "name": "Sticky Note2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1664,
        288
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1056,
        "height": 640,
        "content": "## Validate and build microsite content\n\nSplits the Supabase response into individual records, checks the required company, slug and assessment summary fields, then builds a generic microsite content object. Invalid records are routed to the failure update."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "ecdb218b-e082-441d-937e-7c3937505e2e",
      "name": "Sticky Note3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        2944,
